Defend the physical and chemical treatment account (@wu-physical-chemical-review: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @water-and-sanitation, #water-and-sanitation "../barriers/Membrane-processes-and-the-question-of-separation.lingua#r_2Q10348P8FEN40SJ6SRG12Q8YT") { r_4KVPW53P76JBPM38N5AJRXNBX0
**Read:** Complete the applicable [MIT 1.85](../sources/Water-and-Wastewater-Treatment-Engineering-MIT.lingua#r_396YEC55H29CR6J4ZBZX5JBY60) lectures 3–11 and their associated public assignments; use [The Physics of Water Treatment Design](../sources/Physics-of-Water-Treatment-Design-AguaClara.lingua#r_1V2KMP22J5KMQF65K8Q7ZXXBAR) chapters 2–9 and 11, including derivations and challenges, and [Treatment Plant Performance and Water Quality Data](../sources/Treatment-Plant-Performance-and-Water-Quality-Data.lingua#r_5PZG8VN422GHD657FBDR5KRWGS) for the treatment evidence. Attempt problems before consulting posted answers. The whole-book programme continues through later biological and operational sections.

Present a connected physical/chemical treatment account for the raw-water envelope developed earlier. Explain every unit to a newcomer, derive its simplified model, identify what crosses its boundary, and carry its actual outlet conditions into the next unit. Preserve sludge, spent media, brine, backwash and gas streams. Include chemicals, pumping/mixing power, instruments, isolation, staffing and maintenance demands.

Compare at least two plausible process sequences. Use a quantitative change in flow, temperature or source composition to expose where a nominal design fails. Report net deliverable water under cleaning and unit outages. Distinguish a dimensional estimate, an ideal prediction, experimental validation and evidence from continuing operation.

For advanced work, reproduce a published experiment or public course design, compare competing flow/kinetic models and validate against independent observations or calculations. Demonstrate conservation and numerical convergence, then assess parameter identifiability and source-data uncertainty. A more detailed model is useful only if it answers an identifiable question with evidence.

**Section completion:** Defend the process choice and its limits, including what is still unknown about finished-water stability and microbial barriers. The next development covers membranes, disinfection, distribution and continuing quality; these are not completed by a successful clarification or adsorption calculation. Wastewater, industrial utilities, full-system research and the final water-trail verification also remain distinct work.

**Continue:** [Membrane processes and the question of separation](../barriers/Membrane-processes-and-the-question-of-separation.lingua#r_2Q10348P8FEN40SJ6SRG12Q8YT).
